  "notes": [
    "CPU4 is a lab stress setting on native Apple M1 Pro Metal, not a physical phone. Frame intervals are measured around actual WebGL draw submissions, not GPU completion.",
    "Three sequential baseline and final samples per desktop/mobile-sized viewport; normal motion, identical DPR1 and forced normal quality, fixed simulated noon/clear weather. P95 remains about 17.6ms; no overall FPS or battery claim.",
    "Initial paper is prepared under existing loading alongside assets; optional image wait is bounded at 1500ms after synchronous scene construction. Initial loading was not a paired performance endpoint.",
    "Cache retains one pair of CPU canvases, measured extra raw pixels 2.3-6.4MB across pixel fixtures, no new GPU textures; very long content can exceed these fixture sizes.",
    "Resizing/DPR/chapter changes or a prewarm timeout still use original on-demand capture and can retain a one-time capture stall.",
    "Native Safari, physical phones and long-duration thermal behavior were not tested."
  ],
